    "text": "1. **Helped:** The first batch worked best. `localSearch` for `isRedirectError|getURLFromRedirectError` under `server/` listed every catch site at once (app-render, action-handler, app-route module, make-get-server-inserted-html). Fetching `redirect.ts` in full in the same call gave me the throw side. After that, `localFetch` with line ranges returned exactly the deciding branches: app-render 4386-4403 and 9833-9846, `module.ts` 424-449, and action-handler 1324-1357. Fetching `redirect-error.ts` in full confirmed the digest format.\n\n2. **Did not help:** The `localFetch` call on app-render's range 4375-4410 and 9820-9890 returned more lines than I needed, around 9890. The first `module.ts` range stopped mid-expression at line 445, so I needed a second fetch for 441-455. I never read `make-get-server-inserted-html.tsx`, and I never traced `createRedirectRenderResult` or `RedirectStatusCode`. I also did not check where the status and header are actually flushed after app-render sets them.\n\n3. **Next time:** I would batch slightly wider ranges to avoid the follow-up fetch. I would also read `make-get-server-inserted-html.tsx:50-65` and `createRedirectRenderResult` so those two claims rest on fetched code rather than the doc comment in `redirect.ts`. I would also check where the header is flushed after app-render sets it.\n\n4. **Confidence:** High for the throw mechanism and the three catch sites, since I read the code directly. Medium for the meta-refresh tag and the `x-action-redirect` header, which I took from comments and not from the implementing code.",
